# Environment for this agent. Copy to .env IN THIS DIRECTORY (.secrets/.env — gitignored, managed by
# fastagent) and uncomment what you need. Everything here is OPTIONAL — the defaults work without a .env.

# --- Model auth ---
# Pick auth once: `fastagent login` (an account such as ChatGPT for openai, or an API key),
# or set a provider API key here — the variable name is provider-specific (e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY,
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). `fastagent dev` then lets you choose a model from whatever you're logged into.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Model selection (overrides fastagent.config) ---
# Precedence: --model flag > FASTAGENT_MODEL > config, evaluated in whichever environment is running. This file is
# `dev`'s alone: `fastagent deploy` reads the environment it runs in (or the file `--env-file` names) and never this
# one, and a deployment's values live on its target (`fastagent secrets list <host>`). To fix the model for every instance, set
# `defaults.model` in fastagent.config.ts.
# FASTAGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.5

# --- Serving (fastagent start) ---
# Port precedence: --port > PORT > config.http.port > 8787
# PORT=8787
# These lay over the configuration for what `dev`, `start` and `invoke` run (empty is unset):
# FASTAGENT_THINKING_LEVEL=high
# FASTAGENT_HTTP_API=false
# FASTAGENT_HTTP_PUBLIC_URL=https://agent.example.com
# FASTAGENT_INGRESS=slack=webhook
# Machine-state root: the agent's storage, schedule state, and channel state live under it.
# Default: <agent dir>/.state. Point it at a mounted volume so a redeploy that replaces the
# directory keeps conversations.
# FASTAGENT_STATE_DIR=/data/.state
# Secrets home (this .env + auth.json). Default: <agent dir>/.secrets. Deployments point it at
# the volume so a rotated OAuth credential persists across restarts. Set HERE it moves only
# auth.json — a value inside .env cannot relocate the .env being read.
# FASTAGENT_SECRETS_DIR=/data/.secrets
